From e97969edc73f17cf3e7cea3a6bb1bd7ad881ac18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:11:06 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op player input: the Player's pad reads are wrapped, and
 local players' pads are Npad No.2 to No.4

The other player's Link is to be the game's own Player actor. Four wrapped functions (patch 0005's wraps): the Player's button and stick reads, its input-off check and the controller getter. The module gives another player's Link that player's input there; without it the game's functions run as they are.

Local co-op (split screen): a pad the co-op module hands to a second, third or fourth player on this PC is left out of player 1's merged pad and answers the game's reads of Npad No.2 to No.4 (host/pad_sdl.c keeps each SDL pad's own state; host/nn_hid.c gives those Npads their style and states, and logs once which Npads the game supports). Three exports of the exe for the module, found by name as patch 0008's: hos_coop_pad_info, hos_coop_pad_read and hos_coop_pad_take. Nothing changes until the module takes a pad.
